AB  - This study evaluates the efficiency of code generation by Large Langua
ge Models (LLMs) and measures their performance against human-crafted 
solutions using a dataset from Leetcode. We compare 18 LLMs, consideri
ng factors such as model temperature and success rate, and their impac
t on code performance. This research introduces a novel method for mea
suring and comparing the speed of LLM-generated code, revealing that L
LMs produce code with comparable performance, irrespective of the adop
ted LLM. We also find that LLMs are capable of generating code that is
, on average, more efficient than the code written by humans. The pape
r further discusses the use of Leetcode as a benchmarking dataset, the
 limitations imposed by potential data contamination, and the platform
’s measurement reliability. We believe that our findings contribute to
 a better understanding of LLM capabilities in code generation and set
 the stage for future optimizations in the field.
