AB  - With the rapid development of Large Language Models (LLMs), a large nu
mber of machine learning models have been developed to assist programm
ing tasks including the generation of program code from natural langua
ge input. However, how to evaluate such LLMs for this task is still an
 open problem despite of the great amount of research efforts that hav
e been made and reported to evaluate and compare them. This paper prov
ides a critical review of the existing work on the testing and evaluat
ion of these tools with a focus on two key aspects: the benchmarks and
 the metrics used in the evaluations. Based on the review, further res
earch directions are discussed. 
