AB  - As Large Language Models (LLMs) have shown significant intelligence, t
he progress to leverage LLMs as planning modules of autonomous agents 
has attracted more attention. This survey provides the first systemati
c view of LLM-based agents planning, covering recent works aiming to i
mprove planning ability. We provide a taxonomy of existing works on LL
M-Agent planning, which can be categorized into Task Decomposition, Pl
an Selection, External Module, Reflection and Memory. Comprehensive an
alyses are conducted for each direction, and further challenges for th
e field of research are discussed.
